<title>INDONESIA: Indonesia palm oil markets closed for holiday.</title>
<headline>Indonesia palm oil markets closed for holiday.</headline>
<dateline>JAKARTA 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indonesian palm oil and palm olein markets are closed from February 7 to February 11 for the Moslem Eid al-Fitr celebration.</p>
<p>Olein was quoted at 1,445-50 rupiah in Jakarta on Thursday. Crude palm oil was last sold on Saturday at an equivalent of 1,270 rupiah/kg in a 1,000-tonne tender in Medan.</p>
<p>The market will open again on February 12.</p>
<p>-- Jakarta newsroom +6221 384-6364</p>
</text>
